1️⃣ Build the Kernel Module (.ko)
make
Generates:
    gpio_ctrl.ko → Loadable kernel object
    Intermediate build files (.o, .mod.c, etc.)
2️⃣ Load the Kernel Module
sudo insmod gpio_ctrl.ko
What happens?
    Inserts the module into the kernel
    Executes gpio_init() function
    Allocates major/minor number
3️⃣ Compile User-Space Application
gcc -o user user.c
What happens?
    Compiles the menu-driven user application
    Produces executable:user
4️⃣ Run the User Application
sudo ./user
What you can do:
    Turn LED ON/OFF
    Select GPIO pins
    Read button press count
    Test blocking read
5️⃣ Unload the Kernel Module
sudo rmmod gpio_ctrl
What happens?
    Frees IRQs
    Releases GPIOs
    Removes /dev/gpio_ctrl
    Cleans up kernel resources

Reset counters
